From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: wait for same-queue kbase semaphores on the GPU by default

Binary semaphores pending on the same queue were waited for on the CPU in
vkQueueSubmit. DXVK's per-frame semaphore made every frame wait for the
previous one to finish (~20 ms per frame in NFS Most Wanted). The GPU-wait
path from 059 already handles this case: the new ring entries SYNC_WAIT on
the other subqueues' seqnos. Signal targets cover every subqueue's emitted
seqno, which includes the waited-for targets, so an empty submit still
signals after its waits. PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS=0 restores the CPU
waits.

Purpose: let vkQueueSubmit return after the kick

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Poco X6 Pro)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 (MediaTek)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b (26.3.0-devel)
Validation test: NFS Most Wanted A/B in PanPlay, CTS synchronization + memory + query_pool.statistics_query

Generated-by: LLM
---

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
index 262b218..86ead3d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
@@ -2718,10 +2718,16 @@ panvk_queue_submit_init_signals(struct panvk_queue_submit *submit,
 }
 
 #ifdef HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE
-/* Off by default: G615 query_pool.statistics_query CTS loses the device on
- * subqueue 0 with GPU waits (1-3 of 17769), never with CPU waits. */
+/* Binary semaphores pending on this queue are waited for on the GPU: each
+ * new ring entry SYNC_WAITs for the other subqueues' seqnos, and its own
+ * subqueue is already in order.  The CPU wait this replaces stalled
+ * vkQueueSubmit/vkQueuePresentKHR until the previous frame finished, so the
+ * CPU and GPU never overlapped (NFS Most Wanted: one 20 ms stall per frame).
+ * Signal targets cover every subqueue's emitted seqno, which already
+ * includes the waited-for targets, so an empty submit still signals after
+ * its waits.  PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS=0 restores the CPU waits. */
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(kbase_gpu_semaphore_waits,
-                           "PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS", false)
+                           "PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS", true)
 
 static bool
 kbase_gpu_waits_disabled(void)
